<?xml version="1.0" standalone="yes"?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "unraid-vitals">
<!ENTITY author    "hazemhagrass">
<!ENTITY version   "@VERSION@">
<!ENTITY md5       "@MD5@">
<!ENTITY plugdir   "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY github    "@GITHUB@">
<!ENTITY pkgname   "@PKGNAME@">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/main/plugins/&name;.plg">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
        icon="fa-heartbeat" support="https://forums.unraid.net/topic/TODO-vitals/">

  <CHANGES>
###2026.10.08
- Schedules panel: every job's switch, schedule, last run + duration/exit, Run-now with lock/quiet/parity guards
- Per-agent schedules (disks daily, thermal every 30 min, ...) — agents serialize on one lock
- Retention engine prunes flash rollups, KB docs, research jobs and check results (each with its own keep window)
- Every job has a lock + timeout; the collector no longer stacks slow runs
- Dashboard time ranges filter by real timestamps at any sample interval; UI polling pauses on hidden tabs
###2026.10.07
- One-click full health check: score out of 100, severity-sorted findings, diff vs your previous run (#84)
- Fix playbooks for every check, one click away from any finding (#85)
- Diagnostics export: Unraid's own bundle + an anonymized summary safe for forum posts (#86)
- SMART self-tests per disk from the Hardware tab, with progress and history (#87)
- "What changed?" 14-day timeline: container image tags, plugins, Unraid version, share settings, disk assignments (#88)
###2026.10.06
- Cleanup tab: preview→apply framework with audit log; kinds — plugin logs, tmp, orphaned appdata folders (move-to-held), oversized container logs (truncate), recycle bins (age-filtered), junk files (opted-in shares), docker prune (dangling/unused images, stopped containers, build cache, unused volumes with double confirm)
- Run mover now from the UI: start/stop/status, refuses during parity unless confirmed
- Daily log rotation for the plugin's own logs (5 MiB cap)
###2026.10.05
- Two new diagnosis checks: system maintenance (update checks / NTP / SSD TRIM) and share permissions (files not owned by nobody:users)
- Checks engine: 18 checks; 28 findings live on the reference box, falsification-tested
###2026.10.04
- Vitals is now its own top-level navigation tab, plus a compact tile on the stock Dashboard (headline stats + worst finding)
- Checks engine: 16 built-in health checks with results stored per run
- Agent runtime hardened for headless/reboot: deps auto-provisioned via npm ci,
  SRE vault stub written on install (/root is tmpfs on Unraid and wipes it)
- Plugin payload slimmed to ~250 KB (agent node_modules no longer shipped)
- Durable agent database at /mnt/user/appdata/unraid-vitals/vitals.db
- MVVM agent architecture: service-agnostic sources/providers/core layers
  </CHANGES>

  <!-- Remove any older packaged version before installing the new one. -->
  <FILE Run="/bin/bash">
    <INLINE>
rm -f $(ls /boot/config/plugins/&name;/&name;*.txz 2>/dev/null | grep -v '&version;')
    </INLINE>
  </FILE>

  <!-- Payload. -->
  <FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/&name;/&pkgname;.txz" Run="upgradepkg --install-new">
    <URL>https://github.com/&github;/releases/latest/download/&pkgname;.txz</URL>
    <MD5>&md5;</MD5>
  </FILE>

  <!-- Post-install: config, cron, first sample. -->
  <FILE Run="/bin/bash">
    <INLINE>
&plugdir;/scripts/install.sh
    </INLINE>
  </FILE>

  <!-- Removal. -->
  <FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
    <INLINE>
&plugdir;/scripts/remove.sh
removepkg &pkgname;
rm -rf &plugdir;
    </INLINE>
  </FILE>

</PLUGIN>
